{"time_unix": 1794005556.5882337, "event": "candidate_created", "payload": {"id": "xswap-radix-hole-reclaim-v1", "parent": "5e84ca928deeacb4eee656806a003f27d1eca82f", "parent_commit": "5e84ca928deeacb4eee656806a003f27d1eca82f", "parent_candidate": null, "generation": 1, "baseline_commit": "5e84ca928deeacb4eee656806a003f27d1eca82f", "brief_id": "brief-000001-b31ae8046ca7", "worktree": "worktrees/xswap-radix-hole-reclaim-2026-11-06/xswap-radix-hole-reclaim-v1", "status": "active", "hypothesis": "Replacing flat VM_SPARSE descriptor tables with 2-level RCU radix chunks and asynchronous kfree_rcu() reclamation eliminates interior metadata retention plateaus and synchronize_rcu() latency stalls, compounding Milestones 1 and 2 to pass all 17 correctness gates with >60% metadata memory savings on fragmented swap.", "created_unix": 1794005556.587431, "protocol_sha256": "8202099e5db6fe2a562382db80f28cba5bbbd517e80de9099b4ce906a726b3b2", "mechanism": {"kind": "reviewed_structure", "claim": "In mm/swapfile.c and mm/swap.h, replace flat VM_SPARSE array with 2-level RCU radix chunks: si->cluster_dir[chunk_idx] points to struct swap_cluster_chunk holding 64 swap_cluster_info descriptors, and swap_cluster_lookup_rcu() dereferences via rcu_dereference(). In __free_cluster(), atomic_dec_and_test(&chunk->live_clusters) detects interior empty chunks, scheduling xswap_reclaim_work. The reclaim worker acquires si->xswap_lock and spin_lock(&si->lock), trylocks and unlinks clusters, atomically clears si->cluster_dir[chunk_idx] = NULL, and dispatches asynchronous kfree_rcu(chunk, rcu).", "falsifier": "Exact-tree review shows lost lifetime protection, incorrect slot conflict handling, RCU UAF, lock inversion between si->lock and ci->lock, failure of any of the 17 correctness gates, or latency regression beyond calibrated noise."}}}
